<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.faa-ground-stop-pack</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/faa-ground-stop-pack-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Keeps future-pieces/faa-ground-stop-source-notes.md current, daily, until
       Philip lifts the instruction (15NOV26: "From now on, update the source
       pack daily until further notice").

       Two fires a day, and the second one is the point (16NOV26). At 08:00 CT
       the previous day's FlightAware totals are final and the day's advisory
       index is being written. But 08:00 also evaluates a US traffic day that
       has not started, so the first pass of any date can only report an
       intraday figure; the 23:30 pass replaces that day's block with one whose
       "today" row is nearly closed, and the collector prints the earlier
       reading beside a figure that moved. Measured: Sunday's US cancellations
       read 1,446 at 08:00 on 15NOV26 and 2,336 the next morning.

       08:00 sits after the 06:00 SITREP and before the 09:15 and 09:30
       watchers, so three network jobs do not collide. 23:30 is clear of
       everything.

       An array of dictionaries is supported for StartCalendarInterval; an
       array as the *value* of a key is not. Do not add a RunAtLoad: a login is
       not a new day's data. No model, so no Ollama probe. There is no end date,
       because the instruction is "until further notice" and the guard for that
       is a line in the skill, not a comparison here that would exit 0 forever
       and be forgotten. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>8</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>23</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/faa-ground-stop-pack.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/faa-ground-stop-pack.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
